{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_e6124abb2445496684b49c1d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Generate prompts for spec 002","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","run_in_background":false,"prompt":"Generate dark-factory prompt files from an approved spec.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- **Spec file:** `specs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md` — a path **relative to the repo root**, which is the current working directory (`/workspace`). Do NOT prefix it with `/workspace` in anything you write into the prompt files.\n- **Output directory:** `prompts/` (the inbox — relative to the repo root/cwd). NOT `prompts/in-progress/`; dark-factory moves files on approve.\n- **Mode:** **non-interactive** (daemon-triggered). You MUST NOT call `AskUserQuestion`. Resolve every ambiguity from the spec content alone. If something is genuinely under-specified, still produce the best-effort decomposition and surface the open questions as HTML comments inside the generated prompts so the human reviewer catches them at audit time.\n\nYou have full repo access (cwd = `/workspace`). Verify signatures, look up library APIs, and discover existing patterns BEFORE writing requirements. Do not write a requirement around a symbol you have not grepped.\n\n## Read first\n\n1. The spec in full: `specs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md`.\n2. `docs/verdict-gate.md` — the **authoritative rule set** the gate prompts implement (rules a–k, heading rule, line guard, stale-failure marker, echoed-value and failure-message security rules). This spec's prompt 1 is largely \"implement this doc\".\n3. `specs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md` — the **dependency spec**. Its three prompts are already written and sitting in `prompts/` (`1-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md`, `2-spec-001-repo-clone-script.md`, `3-spec-001-config-allowlist-and-consistency.md`). Read them: they define the scripts, env vars, allowlist string and the three-way consistency test that this spec's prompts build on. Your prompts must not re-create any of that.\n4. The three existing prompt files in `prompts/` — they are the **house style reference** for this repo. Match their structure, tone, frontmatter and section set exactly (`<summary>`, `<objective>`, `<context>`, `<requirements>`, `<verification>`, and the completion-report template dark-factory appends). Note especially how they inline verbatim Go snippets and file contents that are load-bearing.\n5. `docs/observation-scripts.md`, `docs/dod.md`, `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`.\n6. `pkg/factory/factory.go`, `pkg/prompts/prompts.go`, `pkg/prompts/workflow.md`, `pkg/prompts/output-format.md`, and the existing tests `pkg/prompts/prompts_test.go`, `pkg/factory/factory_test.go`, `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go`, `cmd/run-task/main.go`.\n7. The container rules at `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` and the relevant `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-*.md` guides — these govern what the executing YOLO container will and will not do. In particular: prompts must instruct `make test` iteratively and `make precommit` once at the end, must require `github.com/bborbe/errors` wrapping (never `fmt.Errorf`), Ginkgo/Gomega + counterfeiter, ≥80% coverage on new code, and a `## Unreleased` CHANGELOG entry.\n\n## Decomposition\n\nThe spec's `## Suggested Decomposition` table proposes three prompts. Treat it as a strong default, but apply your own sizing judgement:\n\n1. **Verdict gate** — model-output heading rule; gate rules a–k after execution and a–j again at ai_review; removal from the task's *parsed sections* (not a string copy); line guard (symlink resolution on every component, path-inside-clone, file-exists, line-count); stale-`## Failure` removal on completion; all as step wrappers with table tests. Covers AC4–AC7.\n2. **Per-phase prompts** — replace the generic scaffold prompt with `pkg/prompts/planning.md`, `execution.md`, `ai_review.md` (embedded), with content tests. Covers AC8.\n3. **Wiring** — dispatch (`defect-diagnose` in, `llm` out, `healthcheck`/`oauth-probe` still liveness); phase chain with the gate wrappers; the `CreateAgentFromRunner` seam that `CreateAgent` delegates to; wired phase-chain tests (AC3 a–j); README mapping section; CHANGELOG; AC9 greps. Covers AC2, AC3, AC9. Depends on 1 and 2.\n\nName files `1-<slug>.md`, `2-<slug>.md`, `3-<slug>.md` in execution order. Give each a distinct, descriptive slug tied to spec 002 (the spec-001 prompts are already in `prompts/`, so avoid colliding names — the spec-001 files use the `spec-001-` infix; mirror that convention with `spec-002-`).\n\nEvery prompt must carry the frontmatter the existing files use, with `spec: [002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate]` and the branch from the spec frontmatter (`dark-factory/diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate`).\n\n## Hard rules for what you write\n\n- **No dependency on spec 001 having been *executed*** — only on it having been *merged*. The spec says \"Nothing in this spec may start before `read-only-observation-toolkit` is merged\". Prompts 1–3 of spec 001 run before these, so by the time these execute the scripts, env vars and allowlist exist. State this ordering in each prompt's `<context>` rather than re-implementing any of it.\n- **Grep-verify every external symbol** before writing it into a requirement — especially anything from `github.com/bborbe/agent` (v0.89.0 per the spec), `github.com/bborbe/errors`, `github.com/bborbe/run`, `github.com/bborbe/validation`. Module source is at `$(go env GOPATH)/pkg/mod/...`. Read the actual struct definitions with `grep -A 10 \"type X struct\"` before constructing literals. If a symbol the spec cites cannot be verified, do NOT invent it — implement the behaviour in-repo and flag it in an HTML comment.\n- **Inline load-bearing contracts verbatim.** The eight verdict field names and their order, the rule table semantics, the `> `-prefixing rule, the `%q` echoing rule, and the exact reason strings (`does not resolve`, `below High`, `beyond end of file`, `not found in clone`, `resolves outside the clone`, `no line cited; evidence:`, `evidence cites no live read`) must appear in the prompt bodies character-for-character as `docs/verdict-gate.md` states them — the executor's grep is best-effort; verbatim text is zero-effort.\n- **Pin file locations and signatures.** If a new type or function is needed, name it, name its file, and give its signature. Do not leave the executor to invent names.\n- **Single decision per prompt.** Where the spec is ambiguous, pick one design (prefer closest in-repo precedent), commit to it, and record the alternative in an HTML comment as an open question. Never write \"Option A or Option B\".\n- **Fail-loud sentinels for cross-prompt boundaries.** If prompt 3 needs something prompt 1 or 2 shipped, and it is missing, the executor must emit `Status: failed` with an explicit \"not yet deployed (prompt N)\" message — never `needs_input`.\n- **Verification blocks must be runnable as written.** The repo is a Go module; the container runs `make test` iteratively and `make precommit` once. Use the repo's real Makefile targets. Every prompt's `<verification>` must end with `make precommit` and require the completion report to carry `\"verification\":{\"command\":\"make precommit\",\"exitCode\":N}`.\n- **AC10 (the rung-1 live run) is operator-executable** and cannot run in the container. Do not put it in any prompt's `<verification>` as something the container must execute. If it belongs anywhere, it belongs as a clearly-labelled operator note.\n- **Do not add a confidence-threshold knob or a gate opt-out flag** — the spec's Non-goals forbid it explicitly.\n- **Do not touch the `github.com/bborbe/agent` module** or its version — also an explicit Non-goal.\n- **CHANGELOG:** exactly one prompt (the last one) owns the `## Unreleased` entry, since AC9 greps for it. Say so explicitly in the other two prompts so they don't each add one.\n\nReport back: the files you created, the key decisions you made, and every open question you embedded as a comment."}}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"9208e01b-b3f2-4851-90ff-1f42df8e5cd5","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:58:12.203Z"}
