{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a56c0bfa35c1f7a2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstatus: draft\n3\tspec: [001-read-only-observation-toolkit]\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-27T22:45:00Z\"\n5\tbranch: dark-factory/read-only-observation-toolkit\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t# Add the three read-only HTTP observation scripts\n9\t\n10\t<summary>\n11\t\n12\t- The agent image gains three read-only helper scripts the model can call to read task files and metrics.\n13\t- Reading one vault file and listing vault files both go through the vault's HTTP API with a GET only.\n14\t- Querying Prometheus sends exactly one instant query to the fixed query endpoint and nothing else.\n15\t- Each script refuses a malformed argument before it makes any network call.\n16\t- Each script names the missing endpoint setting on stderr instead of failing silently.\n17\t- An HTTP error surfaces its status code on stderr instead of looking like a successful empty read.\n18\t- A huge response is cut off at a fixed size, marked `truncated` on stderr, and still exits 0 so the cut never looks like a failure.\n19\t- Every HTTP call gives up after 30 seconds, so a hanging endpoint cannot stall a task.\n20\t- The behaviour is locked down by tests that drive the real scripts against a local recording HTTP server.\n21\t- Nothing outside the new scripts and their tests changes in this prompt.\n22\t\n23\t</summary>\n24\t\n25\t<objective>\n26\t\n27\tGive the defect diagnoser its first two \"eyes\" on the running system: three executable, read-only HTTP scripts in `agent/scripts/` — `vault-read.sh`, `vault-list.sh`, `prometheus-query.sh` — that behave exactly as `docs/observation-scripts.md` specifies, so that a later diagnosis prompt can read task files and Prometheus metrics without any tool that can write, delete, or reach an arbitrary host. The scripts are the security boundary: every argument is hostile input, and every failure must be visible rather than silent.\n28\t\n29\t</objective>\n30\t\n31\t<context>\n32\t\n33\tRead these before writing anything:\n34\t\n35\t- `docs/observation-scripts.md` — the **authoritative contract** for all three scripts. Read it in full. Where it and any other source disagree, it wins.\n36\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the guardrails prose that tells the model these scripts are its API.\n37\t- `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` — the Config that will allowlist these scripts as `Bash(scripts/<name>.sh:*)`. **Do not edit it in this prompt**; the allowlist change and the consistency test land in a later prompt.\n38\t- `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` and `pkg/factory/factory_test.go` — the repo's Ginkgo/Gomega test idiom (suite file, external `_test` package, counterfeiter not needed here).\n39\t- `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the container's execution rules.\n40\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega suite and spec conventions.\n41\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-precommit.md` — linter limits that apply to test files too (`funlen` 80 lines / 50 statements, `gocognit` 20, `nestif` 4, golines max-len 100).\n42\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-security-linting.md` — gosec expectations (test files are excluded from gosec, so no `#nosec` comments are needed).\n43\t- `docs/dod.md` — the Definition of Done for this repo.\n44\t\n45\tTwo facts about the environment, both verified while writing this prompt:\n46\t\n47\t1. `pkg/scripts/` will contain **only** `_test.go` files in `package scripts_test`. That is a valid Go package: `go test ./...` compiles and runs it. Do **not** add a non-test `.go` file to \"complete\" the package.\n48\t2. The container sets `http_proxy` / `HTTPS_PROXY` in the ambient environment. `curl` honours them, so a loopback request to the test server would be sent to the proxy instead, the recording server would see zero requests, and every \"zero requests\" assertion would silently invert. The test harness must therefore construct the child environment explicitly (see requirement 9).\n49\t\n50\tCreate `pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` with exactly this content. All three prompts in this spec share this one suite file — do not create a second one, and if it already exists with this content leave it untouched:\n51\t\n52\t```go\n53\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n54\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n55\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n56\t\n57\tpackage scripts_test\n58\t\n59\timport (\n60\t\t\"os\"\n61\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n62\t\t\"testing\"\n63\t\t\"time\"\n64\t\n65\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n66\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n67\t\t\"github.com/onsi/gomega/format\"\n68\t)\n69\t\n70\tfunc TestSuite(t *testing.T) {\n71\t\ttime.Local = time.UTC\n72\t\tformat.TruncatedDiff = false\n73\t\tRegisterFailHandler(Fail)\n74\t\tsuiteConfig, reporterConfig := GinkgoConfiguration()\n75\t\tsuiteConfig.Timeout = 60 * time.Second\n76\t\tRunSpecs(t, \"Scripts Suite\", suiteConfig, reporterConfig)\n77\t}\n78\t\n79\t// repoRoot walks up from the test's working directory until it finds go.mod.\n80\tfunc repoRoot() string {\n81\t\tdir, err := os.Getwd()\n82\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n83\t\tfor {\n84\t\t\tif _, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(dir, \"go.mod\")); err == nil {\n85\t\t\t\treturn dir\n86\t\t\t}\n87\t\t\tparent := filepath.Dir(dir)\n88\t\t\tif parent == dir {\n89\t\t\t\tFail(\"go.mod not found above \" + dir)\n90\t\t\t}\n91\t\t\tdir = parent\n92\t\t}\n93\t}\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\t</context>\n97\t\n98\t<requirements>\n99\t\n100\t1. Create `agent/scripts/vault-read.sh`, `agent/scripts/vault-list.sh` and `agent/scripts/prometheus-query.sh`.\n101\t\n102\t   - Each begins with `#!/usr/bin/env bash` and a one-line comment naming what it reads.\n103\t   - Each is marked executable (`chmod +x agent/scripts/*.sh`) — the allowlist entry `Bash(scripts/<name>.sh:*)` resolves to a file the agent executes directly.\n104\t   - Do **not** use `set -e` or `set -u`. `set -u` would abort on an unset endpoint variable before the explicit check can print the variable name.\n105\t   - Do **not** write `${VAR:-…}` anywhere, and do not introduce any environment knob (no clone dir, depth, timeout, output cap, token or gateway secret). The spec forbids env knobs outright.\n106\t\n107\t2. Argument handling, in exactly this order and all of it **before any network call**:\n108\t\n109\t   a. `[ \"$#\" -ne 1 ]` → print the usage line to stderr, `exit 2`.\n110\t   b. Per-script argument validation (requirements 5, 6, 7) → print the rejection reason to stderr, `exit 2`.\n111\t   c. Endpoint presence: `[ -z \"${GIT_REST_URL}\" ]` (or `PROMETHEUS_URL`) → print `GIT_REST_URL is required` / `PROMETHEUS_URL is required` to stderr, `exit 1`.\n112\t\n113\t   Zero arguments and two-or-more arguments must both exit non-zero with zero requests reaching the server.\n114\t\n115\t3. Request shape. Send the response body to a temp file and keep the status in a variable — do **not** pipe `curl`'s body into `head`, because a pipe turns the cut into SIGPIPE and the truncation case would exit non-zero instead of 0. This is the shape, shown with the Prometheus URL and parameter; each script substitutes its own URL, its own parameter name and its own argument:\n116\t\n117\t   ```bash\n118\t   tmp=\"$(mktemp)\"\n119\t   trap 'rm -f \"$tmp\"' EXIT\n120\t   status=\"$(curl -sS --max-time 30 -o \"$tmp\" -w '%{http_code}' \\\n121\t     -G --data-urlencode \"query=${expr}\" \"${PROMETHEUS_URL}/api/v1/query\")\" || {\n122\t     echo \"request failed\" >&2\n123\t     exit 1\n124\t   }\n125\t   ```\n126\t\n127\t   Rules that follow from it:\n128\t\n129\t   - `GET` only. Never pass `-X`, `--request`, `-d`, `--data`, `--data-raw`, `--data-binary`, `--data-ascii`, `--json`, `-F`, `--form`, `-T`, `--upload-file`. `-G --data-urlencode` is the **only** permitted way to send parameters — it is also the only way the read-only check (AC9) accepts.\n130\t   - `--max-time 30` on every `curl` invocation, spelled exactly `--max-time 30` (AC4 greps for that literal).\n131\t\n132\t4. Response handling, identical in all three scripts:\n133\t\n134\t   - Status other than `200` → write the status alone to stderr (so `500` and `401` each appear) and `exit 1`.\n135\t   - Non-zero `curl` exit (transport failure, timeout) → a message on stderr, `exit 1`.\n136\t   - Otherwise read the size as `size=\"$(wc -c < \"$tmp\")\"` and normalise it with `size=\"$((size))\"` (the arithmetic expansion strips the leading whitespace some `wc` builds emit).\n137\t   - `size` greater than `65536` → `head -c 65536 \"$tmp\"` to stdout, `echo truncated >&2`, `exit 0`. The cut must **not** be reported as an error.\n138\t   - `size` at or below `65536` → `cat \"$tmp\"` to stdout, `exit 0`.\n139\t\n140\t5. `vault-read.sh <path>` — read one vault file.\n141\t\n142\t   - Reject with exit 2 when the argument starts with `/`; when `\"/$path/\"` contains the full segment `\"/../\"` (this rejects `../b.md`, `a/../b.md`, `a/..` while still allowing a file legitimately named `a..b.md`); or when the argument contains `?`, `#` or `://`.\n143\t   - Percent-encode before building the URL: `%` → `%25` first, then space → `%20`. No other encoding is needed because validation has already excluded `?`, `#` and `://`.\n144\t   - Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/<encoded path>` with no query string.\n145\t   - Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n146\t\n147\t6. `vault-list.sh <glob>` — list vault files matching a glob.\n148\t\n149\t   - No argument-content validation: the glob travels as a query parameter, not as a path.\n150\t   - Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/` with the query parameter `glob=<glob>`, sent with `-G --data-urlencode`.\n151\t   - Env: `GIT_REST_URL`. The body is written to stdout unchanged (one path per line, empty when nothing matches).\n152\t\n153\t7. `prometheus-query.sh <promql>` — one instant PromQL query.\n154\t\n155\t   - Reject with exit 2 when the argument starts with `/` or contains `://`.\n156\t   - Request: `GET ${PROMETHEUS_URL}/api/v1/query` with the query parameter `query=<promql>`, sent with `-G --data-urlencode`. The path is fixed — no other Prometheus path may be constructed, and no `time` parameter is sent.\n157\t   - Env: `PROMETHEUS_URL`.\n158\t\n159\t8. Create `pkg/scripts/http_scripts_test.go` in `package scripts_test`, using the suite file from `<context>`. It must drive the **real** scripts through the **real** subprocess boundary. Do not re-implement any script logic in Go.\n160\t\n161\t9. Test harness contract:\n162\t\n163\t   - Run the script directly: `exec.CommandContext(ctx, scriptPath, args...)` — not via `bash <script>`. This is how the agent invokes it, and it exercises both the shebang and the executable bit. Use a `context.WithTimeout(ctx, 60*time.Second)`.\n164\t   - Build the child environment explicitly: `PATH` taken from the parent, `HOME` set to a temp directory (so a stray `~/.curlrc` cannot inject a proxy), plus **only** the endpoint variable under test. Never pass `os.Environ()` — the ambient proxy variables would route the loopback request to the proxy and make the recording server record nothing.\n165\t   - Recording server: `httptest.NewServer` whose handler records method, raw request path and raw query, and writes a configurable status and body. Guard the recorded slice with a mutex. Assert on the **raw/escaped** path (`r.URL.EscapedPath()`, or `r.RequestURI`): `r.URL.Path` is already percent-decoded and would hide an unencoded space.\n166\t   - Helpers: `newRecordingServer(t, status int, body string) (*httptest.Server, *recorder)` and `runScript(t, script, env map[string]string, args ...string) (stdout, stderr string, exitCode int)`. Resolve script paths from `repoRoot()`.\n167\t   - Keep every `It` body under ~60 lines by using these helpers; `funlen` (80 lines / 50 statements) and `gocognit` (20) apply to test files too.\n168\t\n169\t10. Test cases — all of them, mirroring the spec's AC2 and AC3:\n170\t\n171\t    **`prometheus-query.sh`**\n172\t\n173\t    - one argument → exactly one request, method `GET`, path `/api/v1/query`, `query` parameter equal to the argument; stdout equals the response body; exit 0.\n174\t    - argument starting with `/` → exit 2 and zero requests; argument containing `://` → exit 2 and zero requests.\n175\t    - zero arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests; two arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests.\n176\t    - `PROMETHEUS_URL` unset → non-zero exit and stderr contains `PROMETHEUS_URL`.\n177\t    - `500` response → non-zero exit with `500` on stderr; `401` response → non-zero exit with `401` on stderr.\n178\t    - 100 KiB response body → stdout is exactly 65536 bytes, stderr contains `truncated`, exit 0.\n179\t\n180\t    **`vault-read.sh`**\n181\t\n182\t    - each of `/etc/passwd`, `../b.md`, `a/../b.md`, `a/..`, `a.md?x=1`, `a.md#x`, `http://evil/x` → exit 2 and zero requests.\n183\t    - `25 Tasks/x y.md` → the recorded raw request path is `/api/v1/files/25%20Tasks/x%20y.md`.\n184\t    - zero arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests; two arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests.\n185\t    - `GIT_REST_URL` unset → non-zero exit and stderr contains `GIT_REST_URL`.\n186\t    - `500` and `401` responses → non-zero exit with the status on stderr.\n187\t    - 100 KiB body → exactly 65536 bytes on stdout, `truncated` on stderr, exit 0.\n188\t\n189\t    **`vault-list.sh`**\n190\t\n191\t    - `* Tasks/*.md` → the recorded `glob` query parameter equals `* Tasks/*.md`, and the request path is `/api/v1/files/`.\n192\t    - zero arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests; two arguments → non-zero exit and zero requests.\n193\t    - `GIT_REST_URL` unset → non-zero exit and stderr contains `GIT_REST_URL`.\n194\t    - `500` and `401` responses → non-zero exit with the status on stderr.\n195\t    - 100 KiB body → exactly 65536 bytes on stdout, `truncated` on stderr, exit 0.\n196\t\n197\t    **All three**\n198\t\n199\t    - every recorded request is a `GET`, and every recorded path is under `/api/v1/files/` (vault scripts) or equals `/api/v1/query` (Prometheus script).\n200\t    - each script file contains the literal `--max-time 30` (AC4's grep, asserted from the test as well).\n201\t\n202\t11. Before finishing, re-run `<verification>` and confirm every line passes. Walk each test case in requirement 10 against the code and confirm it is actually asserted — a test that never asserts a status or a request count does not count as covering the case.\n203\t\n204\t</requirements>\n205\t\n206\t<constraints>\n207\t\n208\t- **Frozen tool names.** The four `Bash(scripts/…)` allowlist entries keep their exact names, resolved relative to the agent working directory. The Dockerfile's existing `COPY agent/ /agent/` ships them.\n209\t- **Script contracts are frozen in `docs/observation-scripts.md`.** A behaviour change updates that page in the same change. Do not change that page in this prompt.\n210\t- **No Go change for env.** `CLAUDE_ENV` / `ClaudeEnvRaw` in `main.go` and `cmd/run-task/main.go` stays exactly as it is. No new flag, field or helper for the two URLs.\n211\t- Do NOT modify `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`, `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `.gitignore` or the `Dockerfile` in this prompt — the allowlist, the prose and the three-way consistency test land in a later prompt.\n212\t- Do NOT create `repo-clone.sh` in this prompt; it is a sibling prompt's deliverable.\n213\t- Do NOT add a `pod-logs.sh` or any pod-log/event read. That waits on the Config CRD gaining a service-account field and is an explicit non-goal.\n214\t- No env knobs of any kind in the scripts: no clone directory, clone depth, timeout, output cap, `GIT_CLONE_TOKEN` or `GATEWAY_SECRET`. These are invariants, not defaults.\n215\t- No private-repo clone auth, no git-rest gateway auth, no Prometheus path other than `/api/v1/query`, no Prometheus range query.\n216\t- Do NOT change the `github.com/bborbe/agent` module. No `go get`, no `go mod tidy` beyond what `make precommit` runs, never `-mod=vendor`.\n217\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n218\t- Existing tests must still pass, and the healthcheck / oauth-probe routing is untouched.\n219\t\n220\t</constraints>\n221\t\n222\t<verification>\n223\t\n224\tRun each command from the repo root. All must pass.\n225\t\n226\t```bash\n227\tmake test          # the new pkg/scripts suite runs here\n228\tmake precommit     # AC1 — must exit 0\n229\t\n230\t# AC4 — each of the three scripts sets a 30 s timeout (count of 1 or more per file)\n231\tgrep -c -- '--max-time 30' agent/scripts/vault-read.sh agent/scripts/vault-list.sh agent/scripts/prometheus-query.sh\n232\t\n233\t# AC9 (curl half) — no curl invocation carries a write verb. The pipeline must print 0.\n234\ttest \"$(sed -e ':a' -e '/\\\\$/N; s/\\\\\\n//; ta' agent/scripts/*.sh | grep -E '(^|[^A-Za-z_])curl ' | grep -cE -- '(-X|--request|--upload-file| -T |--data([^-]|$)|--data-(binary|raw|ascii)|--json| -d | -F |--form)')\" = \"0\"\n235\t\n236\t# AC10 — no env knobs, no defaulted env vars. Both must find nothing.\n237\t! grep -qE 'REPO_CLONE_DIR|GIT_CLONE_DEPTH|GIT_CLONE_TOKEN|GATEWAY_SECRET' agent/scripts/*.sh\n238\t! grep -qE '\\$\\{[A-Z_]+:-' agent/scripts/*.sh\n239\t\n240\t# the three scripts exist and are executable\n241\ttest -x agent/scripts/vault-read.sh && test -x agent/scripts/vault-list.sh && test -x agent/scripts/prometheus-query.sh\n242\t```\n243\t\n244\t</verification>\n245\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"246e4718-5131-4cce-9019-bd896d42a8ce","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:58:19.526Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-afd61a87f56e715a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstatus: draft\n3\tspec: [001-read-only-observation-toolkit]\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-27T22:45:00Z\"\n5\tbranch: dark-factory/read-only-observation-toolkit\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t# Align the Config allowlist, image and prose, and enforce the agreement with a test\n9\t\n10\t<summary>\n11\t\n12\t- The Config's tool allowlist stops naming a script that cannot work and matches the four scripts that exist.\n13\t- The vault and Prometheus addresses now reach the model through the channel the runner actually forwards, instead of sitting in pod env where they were silently dropped.\n14\t- The dead plain-environment keys for those two addresses are gone.\n15\t- The Config's comments describe the deferred Kubernetes read path in the same words the README uses.\n16\t- The container image ships `git`, so the clone script can run at all.\n17\t- A local clone directory cannot be committed by accident.\n18\t- The guardrails and the README describe the two read paths that actually exist, and the README no longer advises a code change for something the Config already handles.\n19\t- A test fails the build if the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the prose ever disagree in any direction.\n20\t- The changelog records the change.\n21\t\n22\t</summary>\n23\t\n24\t<objective>\n25\t\n26\tClose the gap between what the Config claims and what the image actually contains. Today the Config allowlists five scripts, none of which exists, one of which (`pod-logs.sh`) cannot work on the current platform; it also sets the two endpoint URLs as plain pod env, which the Claude runner strips before spawning the model — so even a correct script would fail with \"variable is required\" while `kubectl describe pod` shows the variable set. After this change the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the prompt/guardrail prose agree in every direction, and a test enforces that agreement so the next drift fails `make test` instead of failing at runtime.\n27\t\n28\t</objective>\n29\t\n30\t<context>\n31\t\n32\tRead these before writing anything:\n33\t\n34\t- `docs/observation-scripts.md` — the **authoritative contract** for the scripts. Read the \"How the scripts get their env\" section in full; it names the exact Config value this prompt commits.\n35\t- `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` — the Config being edited.\n36\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the guardrails prose being edited.\n37\t- `README.md` — the Env Vars table and the \"Claude subprocess env allowlist\" section.\n38\t- `CHANGELOG.md` — the file to append an `## Unreleased` section to.\n39\t- `Dockerfile` — the `apk --no-cache add` line that must gain `git`. Note the final stage is `FROM alpine`, which resolves to the earlier stage **named** `alpine`, so packages installed in that stage do ship in the image.\n40\t- `.gitignore` — the file to extend.\n41\t- `main.go` and `cmd/run-task/main.go` — read them to confirm the claim that no Go change is needed: both already parse `CLAUDE_ENV` (`env:\"CLAUDE_ENV\"`, arg `-claude-env`) through `envparse.KeyValuePairs` into the runner's env map. **Do not edit either file.**\n42\t- `pkg/prompts/workflow.md`, `pkg/prompts/output-format.md` — the embedded prompts the consistency test scans for script mentions.\n43\t- `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` and `pkg/factory/factory_test.go` — the repo's Ginkgo/Gomega test idiom.\n44\t- `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the container's execution rules.\n45\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/changelog-guide.md` — entry format and the required `feat:`/`fix:`/… prefix.\n46\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega conventions.\n47\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-precommit.md` — linter limits that apply to test files too (`funlen` 80 lines / 50 statements, `gocognit` 20, `nestif` 4, golines max-len 100).\n48\t- `docs/dod.md` — the Definition of Done for this repo (it explicitly requires the CHANGELOG entry and the docs update).\n49\t\n50\t`pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` already exists from a sibling prompt in this spec and defines `repoRoot()`. **Leave it untouched**, do not create a second suite file (two `RunSpecs` calls in one package fail the build), and do not redefine `repoRoot()`.\n51\t\n52\t<!-- Two deliberate deviations from the spec's literal AC text, both preserving the AC's intent:\n53\t\n54\t     1. AC7/AC11 write the leading whitespace as `\\s`. `[[:space:]]` is used here instead:\n55\t        portable across grep builds and asserts the identical thing.\n56\t\n57\t     2. AC8's exact-string check is written in the spec as `grep -c '<allowlist>'`. Plain\n58\t        `grep` is BRE, where `*` is a quantifier — the pattern `Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*)`\n59\t        compiles to \"…vault-read.sh\" + zero-or-more `:` + \")\", which does NOT match the file\n60\t        and returns 0, so the AC's stated `1` is unreachable with that exact command.\n61\t        `grep -cF` (fixed string) returns the intended 1 and is verified to do so. -->\n62\t\n63\t</context>\n64\t\n65\t<requirements>\n66\t\n67\t1. **`k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`** — three edits, nothing else in the file changes. The `NOT APPLIED` header, the `metadata`/`spec` values, `taskTypes`, `resources`, `secretName` and the `ANTHROPIC_*` keys all stay as they are.\n68\t\n69\t   a. Replace the `ALLOWED_TOOLS` value. Old → new:\n70\t\n71\t   ```yaml\n72\t   # old\n73\t   ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/pod-logs.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)\"\n74\t   # new — the `pod-logs.sh` entry is dropped; the four surviving names are unchanged\n75\t   ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)\"\n76\t   ```\n77\t\n78\t   b. Delete the plain `GIT_REST_URL:` and `PROMETHEUS_URL:` keys from `spec.env` and add `CLAUDE_ENV` in their place. The `CLAUDE_ENV` line must be indented, end immediately after the closing quote (no trailing comment on that line), and hold exactly:\n79\t\n80\t   ```yaml\n81\t   CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"\n82\t   ```\n83\t\n84\t   Replace the surrounding comments so they explain the mechanism rather than the old state — the current comment still says the scripts are \"not yet written — domain work\", which is no longer true, and the current endpoint comments sit on the two keys being deleted. Say that the Claude runner strips pod env down to a fixed allowlist, so the endpoint URLs reach the scripts only through `CLAUDE_ENV`, a comma-separated `KEY=VALUE` list parsed by both entry points.\n85\t\n86\t   c. Rewrite the trailing comment block about read path 3. It must contain the exact phrase `Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2`, must keep the substance about the missing `serviceAccount` field and the gated RBAC, and must not contain the string `Pod logs` (the platform cannot read pod logs, which is why the script is being dropped). Keep `pods/log` out of the phrase \"Pod logs\" — describing the ServiceAccount's future permissions is fine.\n87\t\n88\t2. **`Dockerfile`** — add `git` to the existing `apk --no-cache add` line, keeping the rest of the package list and the trailing backslash intact. No other Dockerfile change.\n89\t\n90\t3. **`.gitignore`** — ensure it contains exactly one line `/agent/repos/` (leading slash, so it anchors to the repo root and does not shadow anything else). A sibling prompt may already have added it because its tests create the directory: if the line is present, leave it alone; if it is absent, add it; never duplicate it. Leave the other entries as they are.\n91\t\n92\t4. **`agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`** — one edit: the domain bullet that reads \"(task files, Prometheus, pod logs/events)\" becomes \"(task files, Prometheus)\". Nothing else in the file changes; the `## Forbidden` section stays exactly as it is, and the scripts remain the sole exception to the internal-network rule.\n93\t\n94\t5. **`README.md`** — three edits.\n95\t\n96\t   a. The \"Observes\" bullet (currently \"task files → Prometheus → pod logs/events via its own read-only service account\") becomes:\n97\t\n98\t   ```markdown\n99\t   - **Observes (read-only, in order):** task files → Prometheus (Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2)\n100\t   ```\n101\t\n102\t   The phrase `task files → Prometheus` must survive verbatim, and the deferred wording must be the same phrase used in the Config.\n103\t\n104\t   b. Rewrite the `### Claude subprocess env allowlist` section. Keep the heading verbatim. Keep the warning that the runner strips pod env down to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...`) so a variable visible in `kubectl describe pod` can still be absent from the subprocess. Replace the advice to thread variables through `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` in `main.go` — the string `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` must not appear anywhere in the file afterwards. Name `CLAUDE_ENV` as the channel: a comma-separated `KEY=VALUE` list set on the Config's `spec.env` (or `-claude-env` for a local run) and parsed by both entry points. Include one line that contains `CLAUDE_ENV` and both endpoints, for example:\n105\t\n106\t   ```markdown\n107\t   `CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"`\n108\t   ```\n109\t\n110\t   c. Link `docs/observation-scripts.md` from the README — at minimum from the rewritten section, and add it to the `## Related` list.\n111\t\n112\t   Leave the generic `Tune ALLOWED_TOOLS per task shape` example table alone: it illustrates other agents' tool sets (`vault-write.sh`, `trading-api-read.sh`) and is not a claim about this agent.\n113\t\n114\t6. **`CHANGELOG.md`** — add an `## Unreleased` section above `## v0.0.0` with one bullet describing what was implemented. Follow `changelog-guide.md`: the entry needs a `feat:` prefix and must mention \"observation scripts\". Do not describe verification steps, and do not use the prompt filename.\n115\t\n116\t7. **`pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go`** (`package scripts_test`, using the existing suite file and `repoRoot()`) — the three-way agreement test. It must parse the Config rather than hard-coding a copy of the allowlist:\n117\t\n118\t   a. Read `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` and extract the `ALLOWED_TOOLS` value with a regex equivalent to `(?m)^\\s*ALLOWED_TOOLS:\\s*\"(.*)\"\\s*$`. Fail loudly if it does not match — a silently empty allowlist would make every check below vacuous.\n119\t\n120\t   b. Split the value on `,` and collect the entries matching `^Bash\\(scripts/(.+):\\*\\)$`, keeping the captured script name. Compare the captured names as plain strings — never by re-grepping the file, because a shell `grep` pattern containing `:*` is a BRE quantifier and would silently match nothing.\n121\t\n122\t   c. Assert that set equals exactly `{vault-read.sh, vault-list.sh, prometheus-query.sh, repo-clone.sh}`, so an emptied or renamed allowlist cannot pass vacuously.\n123\t\n124\t   d. For every allowlisted script name, assert `agent/scripts/<name>` exists and is executable.\n125\t\n126\t   e. Walk `agent/scripts/`; for every regular file with any executable bit set, assert an allowlist entry names it. This is the direction that catches a new script nobody allowlisted.\n127\t\n128\t   f. Read `pkg/prompts/*.md` and `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`; find every `scripts/<name>.sh` mention with a regex equivalent to `scripts/([A-Za-z0-9._-]+\\.sh)`; assert each mentioned name has an allowlist entry. This is the direction that catches prose pointing at a tool that does not exist.\n129\t\n130\t   g. Assert no case-insensitive match of `pod[- ]?logs` in any of: `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`, `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, and every `pkg/prompts/*.md`. This is the negative half of the agreement: the dropped tool must not linger in prose or comments.\n131\t\n132\t   h. Assert the Config's `CLAUDE_ENV` value — extracted with a regex equivalent to `(?m)^\\s*CLAUDE_ENV:\\s*\"(.*)\"\\s*$` — parses into both keys. Mirror the call in `main.go` (`claudeEnv := envparse.KeyValuePairs(a.ClaudeEnvRaw)`): read that line first to confirm the import path, the call form and the result type, then use the same call here and assert the map contains `GIT_REST_URL` and `PROMETHEUS_URL` with the values `http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090` and `http://prometheus.monitoring:9090`. This is the container-side guard for the seam that the operator-side acceptance check proves on the host: a Config value that greps correctly but parses into one key would otherwise ship.\n133\t\n134\t   Note that `README.md` is deliberately **not** part of check (f): its example allowlist table names scripts belonging to other agents.\n135\t\n136\t8. Keep every `It` body under ~60 lines; factor shared reading/parsing into helpers so `funlen` (80 lines / 50 statements) and `gocognit` (20) pass.\n137\t\n138\t9. Before finishing, re-run `<verification>` and confirm every line passes. Walk requirements 1–7 against the files you changed and confirm each exact string is present (or absent, where the requirement is a removal).\n139\t\n140\t</requirements>\n141\t\n142\t<constraints>\n143\t\n144\t- **Frozen tool names.** The four `Bash(scripts/…)` allowlist entries keep their exact names, resolved relative to the agent working directory. The Dockerfile's existing `COPY agent/ /agent/` ships them.\n145\t- **Script contracts are frozen in `docs/observation-scripts.md`.** A behaviour change updates that page in the same change. Do not change that page in this prompt.\n146\t- **No Go change for env.** `CLAUDE_ENV` / `ClaudeEnvRaw` in `main.go` and `cmd/run-task/main.go` stays exactly as it is. No new flag, field or helper for the two URLs.\n147\t- `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` keeps its `NOT APPLIED` header. Only `ALLOWED_TOOLS`, the env keys and the path-3 comments change.\n148\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` § Forbidden is unchanged. The scripts remain the sole exception to the internal-network rule.\n149\t- Do NOT add a `pod-logs.sh`, a pod-log/event read, or any replacement for it. It waits on the Config CRD gaining a service-account field and is an explicit non-goal.\n150\t- No `kubectl apply`, deploy, secret manifest or RBAC. The Config file stays NOT APPLIED.\n151\t- Do NOT change the `github.com/bborbe/agent` module. No `go get`, never `-mod=vendor`.\n152\t- Do NOT create or modify the scripts under `agent/scripts/` — they are sibling prompts' deliverables, and this prompt only reads them. Do not edit `pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` or the sibling test files.\n153\t- AC12 (proving the env reaches the Claude subprocess) is operator-verified on the host after merge, against the router token and the committed Config value; it is not reproducible in this container. Do not attempt it and do not add it to `<verification>`.\n154\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n155\t- Existing tests must still pass, and the healthcheck / oauth-probe routing is untouched.\n156\t\n157\t</constraints>\n158\t\n159\t<verification>\n160\t\n161\tRun each command from the repo root. Every line must pass.\n162\t\n163\t```bash\n164\tmake test          # the consistency test runs here\n165\tmake precommit     # AC1 — must exit 0\n166\t```\n167\t\n168\t**AC7 — env forwarding (all four must pass):**\n169\t\n170\t```bash\n171\ttest \"$(grep -cE '^[[:space:]]+CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"$' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" = \"1\"\n172\ttest \"$(grep -cE 'CLAUDE_ENV: .*GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" = \"1\"\n173\ttest \"$(grep -cE 'CLAUDE_ENV: .*PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" = \"1\"\n174\t! grep -qE '^[[:space:]]+(GIT_REST_URL|PROMETHEUS_URL):' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml\n175\t```\n176\t\n177\t**AC8 — allowlist, scripts and prose agree:**\n178\t\n179\t```bash\n180\t# `-F` because the allowlist contains `(`, `)` and `*`, which plain grep reads as BRE metacharacters\n181\ttest \"$(grep -cF 'ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)\"' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" = \"1\"\n182\t! grep -qiE 'pod[- ]?logs' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md README.md pkg/prompts/*.md\n183\t```\n184\t\n185\t**AC11 — image, hygiene and docs:**\n186\t\n187\t```bash\n188\tgrep -qE 'apk .*add.* git( |$)' Dockerfile\n189\ttest \"$(grep -c '^/agent/repos/' .gitignore)\" = \"1\"\n190\ttest \"$(grep -c 'docs/observation-scripts.md' README.md)\" -ge 1\n191\ttest \"$(grep -cE 'CLAUDE_ENV.*(GIT_REST_URL|PROMETHEUS_URL)' README.md)\" -ge 1\n192\ttest \"$(grep -c 'task files → Prometheus' README.md)\" = \"1\"\n193\ttest \"$(grep -c 'Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\" -ge 1\n194\ttest \"$(grep -c 'Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2' README.md)\" -ge 1\n195\t! grep -q 'ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env' README.md\n196\ttest \"$(sed -n '/^### Claude subprocess env allowlist/,/^## /p' README.md | grep -c 'CLAUDE_ENV')\" -ge 1\n197\ttest \"$(grep -c '(task files, Prometheus)' agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md)\" = \"1\"\n198\ttest \"$(sed -n '/^## Unreleased/,/^## v/p' CHANGELOG.md | grep -ci 'observation scripts')\" -ge 1\n199\t```\n200\t\n201\t</verification>\n202\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"157b20e3-def7-4022-9cc8-ce38058693fe","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:58:19.528Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
