{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab661926ce7c385e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstatus: draft\n3\tspec: [001-read-only-observation-toolkit]\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-27T22:45:00Z\"\n5\tbranch: dark-factory/read-only-observation-toolkit\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t# Add the read-only repo-clone script with a traversal and symlink guard\n9\t\n10\t<summary>\n11\t\n12\t- The agent image gains one script that makes a read-only local clone of a public source repo.\n13\t- Only `owner/name`-shaped references to GitHub are accepted; every other shape is refused.\n14\t- A crafted reference containing shell metacharacters, a scheme, or a `..` segment is refused before anything runs.\n15\t- A directory pre-planted as a symlink inside the clone root cannot be used to escape it.\n16\t- Every refusal happens before `git` runs and before any file is created, removed or changed.\n17\t- Re-cloning over a previous read-only tree works for a non-root user.\n18\t- A finished clone is non-writable, so the model cannot modify or push what it read.\n19\t- The clone reports the local path, the commit it landed on, and the default branch.\n20\t- The local clone directory is ignored by git, so a test run cannot commit a nested clone.\n21\t- The behaviour is locked down by tests that use a stub `git` and compare before/after filesystem snapshots.\n22\t\n23\t</summary>\n24\t\n25\t<objective>\n26\t\n27\tGive the defect diagnoser its fourth read-only eye: `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`, which clones a public GitHub repo into a fixed `repos/` directory beside the scripts so a later diagnosis prompt can read real source at a real commit. The script is the security boundary — its argument comes from a model that has read untrusted task text and untrusted repo content, so a crafted reference must never reach another host, another path, or a destructive filesystem call.\n28\t\n29\t</objective>\n30\t\n31\t<context>\n32\t\n33\tRead these before writing anything:\n34\t\n35\t- `docs/observation-scripts.md` — the **authoritative contract**, section `repo-clone.sh clone <repo>`. Read it in full. Where it and any other source disagree, it wins.\n36\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the guardrails prose that tells the model these scripts are its API.\n37\t- `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` — the Config that will allowlist this script as `Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)`. **Do not edit it in this prompt.**\n38\t- `.gitignore` — you add one line to it (requirement 1).\n39\t- `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` and `pkg/factory/factory_test.go` — the repo's Ginkgo/Gomega test idiom.\n40\t- `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the container's execution rules.\n41\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega suite and spec conventions.\n42\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-precommit.md` — linter limits that apply to test files too (`funlen` 80 lines / 50 statements, `gocognit` 20, `nestif` 4, golines max-len 100).\n43\t- `docs/dod.md` — the Definition of Done for this repo.\n44\t\n45\t**The upstream reference is not available.** The spec says this contract closes a `..` traversal hole in `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/repo-clone.sh`. That repo is **not** reachable from this container and is not vendored. Do not guess at its contents and do not copy from it — implement only what `docs/observation-scripts.md` specifies.\n46\t\n47\tThree facts about the environment, all verified while writing this prompt:\n48\t\n49\t1. `pkg/scripts/` will contain **only** `_test.go` files in `package scripts_test`. That is a valid Go package: `go test ./...` compiles and runs it. Do **not** add a non-test `.go` file.\n50\t2. `pkg/scripts/scripts_suite_test.go` is shared with a sibling prompt that adds the HTTP-script tests. **If it already exists, leave it untouched.** If it does not exist, create it with exactly this content — and never create a second suite file, because two `RunSpecs` calls in one package fail the build:\n51\t\n52\t```go\n53\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n54\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n55\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n56\t\n57\tpackage scripts_test\n58\t\n59\timport (\n60\t\t\"os\"\n61\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n62\t\t\"testing\"\n63\t\t\"time\"\n64\t\n65\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n66\t\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n67\t\t\"github.com/onsi/gomega/format\"\n68\t)\n69\t\n70\tfunc TestSuite(t *testing.T) {\n71\t\ttime.Local = time.UTC\n72\t\tformat.TruncatedDiff = false\n73\t\tRegisterFailHandler(Fail)\n74\t\tsuiteConfig, reporterConfig := GinkgoConfiguration()\n75\t\tsuiteConfig.Timeout = 60 * time.Second\n76\t\tRunSpecs(t, \"Scripts Suite\", suiteConfig, reporterConfig)\n77\t}\n78\t\n79\t// repoRoot walks up from the test's working directory until it finds go.mod.\n80\tfunc repoRoot() string {\n81\t\tdir, err := os.Getwd()\n82\t\tExpect(err).NotTo(HaveOccurred())\n83\t\tfor {\n84\t\t\tif _, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(dir, \"go.mod\")); err == nil {\n85\t\t\t\treturn dir\n86\t\t\t}\n87\t\t\tparent := filepath.Dir(dir)\n88\t\t\tif parent == dir {\n89\t\t\t\tFail(\"go.mod not found above \" + dir)\n90\t\t\t}\n91\t\t\tdir = parent\n92\t\t}\n93\t}\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\t`repoRoot()` is defined there. Use it; do **not** redefine it in your test file.\n97\t\n98\t3. The tests write real clone trees into `<repo>/agent/repos/`, because the clone root is fixed beside the scripts. That is why requirement 1 adds the ignore line: dark-factory commits whatever is in the worktree, and a leftover clone must never be committed.\n99\t\n100\t</context>\n101\t\n102\t<requirements>\n103\t\n104\t1. Create `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`: `#!/usr/bin/env bash` plus a one-line comment, marked executable (`chmod +x`). Do **not** use `set -e` or `set -u`, and do **not** write `${VAR:-…}` or introduce any environment knob (no clone dir, depth, timeout, token or gateway secret — the spec forbids env knobs outright).\n105\t\n106\t   Also add the single line `/agent/repos/` to `.gitignore` (leading slash, anchored to the repo root), leaving the existing entries untouched. This is deliberately part of this prompt rather than the later Config/prose prompt: this prompt's tests are what create the directory, and a clone tree left behind by a killed test run would otherwise be committed.\n107\t\n108\t2. Subcommand handling, before anything else:\n109\t\n110\t   - `[ \"$#\" -ne 2 ]` → print the usage line (`usage: repo-clone.sh clone <owner>/<name>`) to stderr, `exit 2`.\n111\t   - `[ \"$1\" != \"clone\" ]` → the same usage line to stderr, `exit 2`. There is no `log` subcommand and no other subcommand.\n112\t\n113\t3. Normalise the reference to `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>`:\n114\t\n115\t   - `https://github.com/<rest>` → slug `<rest>`.\n116\t   - `git@github.com:<rest>` → slug `<rest>`.\n117\t   - any other argument containing `://` → usage, `exit 2` (this catches `http://evil.example/x/y` and `file:///etc/x`).\n118\t   - anything else → slug is the argument unchanged.\n119\t   - strip one trailing `.git` from the slug.\n120\t   - split the slug on the **first** `/`: a slug with no `/` is invalid (`exit 2`), and a name that still contains a `/` is invalid (`exit 2`).\n121\t\n122\t4. Validation — all of it before `git` runs and before the filesystem is touched. Every failure prints `invalid repo reference` to stderr and exits 2:\n123\t\n124\t   - `owner` and `name` are each non-empty and each contain only characters from `A-Za-z0-9._-`.\n125\t   - neither `owner` nor `name` is `.` or `..`.\n126\t   - **Defence in depth:** the destination `<agent dir>/repos/<owner>/<name>`, resolved with symlinks followed, lies strictly inside the resolved `<agent dir>/repos/`.\n127\t     - Resolve the parent: if `<repos>/<owner>` exists or is a symlink, resolve it with `cd \"<repos>/<owner>\" && pwd -P`; otherwise resolve `<repos>` physically (or the agent dir when `repos/` does not exist yet) and append the literal `<owner>`. Then append `/<name>` and require the result to sit under the resolved `<repos>/`.\n128\t     - This check must **not create anything** — no `mkdir`, no `rm -rf`, no `chmod` before it. Creating the owner directory would follow a planted symlink and write outside `repos/`, which the snapshot assertions catch.\n129\t\n130\t5. The clone root is fixed: the `repos/` directory beside `scripts/`. Derive it from the script's own location with symlinks followed:\n131\t\n132\t   ```bash\n133\t   script_dir=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd -P)\"\n134\t   agent_dir=\"$(cd \"$script_dir/..\" && pwd -P)\"\n135\t   repos_dir=\"$agent_dir/repos\"\n136\t   ```\n137\t\n138\t   No env override, no argument, no default.\n139\t\n140\t6. Replacing an existing clone: when the destination exists or is a symlink, first `chmod -R u+w \"$dest\"` (tolerate failure), then `rm -rf \"$dest\"`, then `mkdir -p` the owner directory. Restoring write permission first is what makes a re-clone over the previous read-only tree succeed for a non-root user.\n141\t\n142\t7. Clone with exactly `git clone \"$url\" \"$dest\"` where `url` is `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>`. No `--recurse-submodules`, no other flags, no credentials, no submodules.\n143\t\n144\t8. Any non-zero `git clone` exit → print `git clone failed for <url>` to stderr and exit non-zero.\n145\t\n146\t9. On success:\n147\t\n148\t   - `head_sha` from `git -C \"$dest\" rev-parse HEAD` and `default_branch` from `git -C \"$dest\" rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`, each tolerated to fail (suppress stderr, do not abort) so an unusual tree cannot fail the script.\n149\t   - Make the whole tree, `.git` included, non-writable: `chmod -R a-w \"$dest\"` (only when the destination exists).\n150\t   - Write to stdout, flat `key=value`, all three lines unconditionally: `clone_path=<absolute path>`, `head_sha=<sha>`, `default_branch=<branch>`.\n151\t\n152\t10. Create `pkg/scripts/stub_git_test.go` (the stub helper) and `pkg/scripts/repo_clone_test.go` (the specs), both in `package scripts_test`. Use the shared suite file from `<context>`; do not create a second suite file and do not redefine `repoRoot()`.\n153\t\n154\t11. Stub `git` contract — the test writes an executable shell script named `git` into a temp directory and prepends that directory to the child's `PATH`:\n155\t\n156\t    - it appends its full argv to the log file named by `STUB_GIT_LOG`;\n157\t    - when `$1` is `clone`, it `mkdir -p`s the **last** argument (the destination), counts the `clone ` lines already in the log to get the call index, writes `<dest>/stub-clone-marker-<index>`, and exits with `$STUB_GIT_CLONE_EXIT` (default 0);\n158\t    - for any other subcommand it exits 0 printing nothing.\n159\t\n160\t    Consequences the tests rely on: the `clone ` lines in the log are the assertion target (the script's later `rev-parse` calls also get logged, so filter on the `clone ` prefix); and a second clone removes the first call's marker because the script `rm -rf`s the destination before cloning again.\n161\t\n162\t12. Build the child environment explicitly for every invocation: `PATH` = stub directory + the parent's `PATH`, `HOME` = a temp directory, plus the `STUB_GIT_*` variables. Never pass `os.Environ()` — the container sets `http_proxy` / `HTTPS_PROXY`, and passing them through makes `curl`/`git` route loopback traffic to the proxy. Run the script directly with `exec.CommandContext(ctx, scriptPath, args...)` under a `context.WithTimeout(ctx, 60*time.Second)`.\n163\t\n164\t13. Snapshot helper: record path plus mode bits for everything under `<agent dir>` excluding `repos/`, plus the outside-target directory used by the symlink case (`find … -printf '%p %m\\n' | sort`; GNU find is available). Compare the string before and after each case.\n165\t\n166\t14. Resolve the expected destination with symlinks followed, so the comparison is stable: `agentDir, _ := filepath.EvalSymlinks(filepath.Join(repoRoot(), \"agent\"))` then `filepath.Join(agentDir, \"repos\", \"bborbe\", \"foo\")`. The script resolves its own path with `pwd -P`, so a logical-path comparison would flake on a symlinked checkout.\n167\t\n168\t15. Test cases — all of them, mirroring the spec's AC5 and AC6:\n169\t\n170\t    **Rejections** — for each of `evil`, `a;b/c`, `http://evil.example/x/y`, `file:///etc/x`, `../x`, `x/..`, `x/.`, `./.`, `../..`, `https://github.com/../x`, `git@github.com:x/...git`: exit 2, **zero** stub-git invocations, and identical before/after snapshots.\n171\t\n172\t    **Symlink escape** — create a temp directory outside `repos/` holding a sentinel file; plant `<agent dir>/repos/evil` as a symlink to it; run `clone evil/x`. Assert exit 2, zero stub-git invocations, stderr containing `invalid repo reference`, the sentinel file still present, `agent/repos/evil` still a symlink, and identical before/after snapshots. This is the case that fails if validation creates the owner directory before resolving it.\n173\t\n174\t    **Success** — `clone bborbe/foo`: exactly one `clone` invocation, whose logged argv is `clone https://github.com/bborbe/foo <expected dest>`; no `--recurse-submodules` anywhere in the log; stdout carries an absolute `clone_path=` inside `<agent dir>/repos/`, plus `head_sha=` and `default_branch=` lines; `find <clone> -perm -u+w` prints nothing.\n175\t\n176\t    **Dotted owner** — `clone bborbe/.github`: accepted, exactly one `clone` invocation.\n177\t\n178\t    **Second clone** — run `clone bborbe/foo` twice against the same log: the second exits 0, the log shows two `clone` invocations, `stub-clone-marker-1` is gone and `stub-clone-marker-2` is present. **Skip this spec when `os.Geteuid() == 0`** with a message naming the blind spot: root removes a read-only tree without needing the permission restoration, so on uid 0 the spec proves nothing about the restoration path. The mode-bit assertions (the `find -perm -u+w` check) hold under any uid and must not be skipped.\n179\t\n180\t    **Clone failure** — `STUB_GIT_CLONE_EXIT=128`: non-zero exit and `git clone failed` on stderr.\n181\t\n182\t    **Bad subcommand** — `log x y`: exit 2 with the usage line on stderr.\n183\t\n184\t16. Cleanup: an `AfterEach` must restore write permission before removing the tree — `chmod -R u+w <agent dir>/repos`, then `os.RemoveAll`. Without the `chmod`, the read-only tree survives the run and pollutes the working tree. After `make test`, `agent/repos` must be empty or absent.\n185\t\n186\t17. Keep every `It` body under ~60 lines by using helpers for the snapshot, the stub setup and the script invocation; `funlen` (80 lines / 50 statements) and `gocognit` (20) apply to test files too.\n187\t\n188\t18. Before finishing, re-run `<verification>` and confirm every line passes. Walk each case in requirement 15 against the code and confirm it is actually asserted — a rejection case that does not assert both the exit code and the invocation count does not count as covering the case.\n189\t\n190\t</requirements>\n191\t\n192\t<constraints>\n193\t\n194\t- **Frozen tool names.** The four `Bash(scripts/…)` allowlist entries keep their exact names, resolved relative to the agent working directory. The Dockerfile's existing `COPY agent/ /agent/` ships them.\n195\t- **Script contracts are frozen in `docs/observation-scripts.md`.** A behaviour change updates that page in the same change. Do not change that page in this prompt.\n196\t- The clone root is the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` (`/agent/repos` in the image, `agent/repos/` in a local checkout). No env override — that is an explicit non-goal.\n197\t- No `repo-clone.sh log` subcommand. Nothing in v1 consumes regression history.\n198\t- No private-repo clone auth (`GIT_CLONE_TOKEN` / GitHub App) and no git-rest gateway auth (`GATEWAY_SECRET`). v1 clones only repos reachable without credentials.\n199\t- **No Go change for env.** `CLAUDE_ENV` / `ClaudeEnvRaw` in `main.go` and `cmd/run-task/main.go` stays exactly as it is.\n200\t- The only files outside `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh` and `pkg/scripts/` that this prompt touches are `.gitignore` (the single `/agent/repos/` line) and nothing else. Do NOT modify `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`, `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` or the `Dockerfile` — the allowlist, the prose and the three-way consistency test land in a later prompt.\n201\t- Do NOT create the three HTTP scripts (`vault-read.sh`, `vault-list.sh`, `prometheus-query.sh`) in this prompt; they are a sibling prompt's deliverable. The suite file in `<context>` is the only shared file, and it must not be duplicated.\n202\t- Do NOT add a `pod-logs.sh` or any pod-log/event read. That waits on the Config CRD gaining a service-account field and is an explicit non-goal.\n203\t- Do NOT change the `github.com/bborbe/agent` module. No `go get`, never `-mod=vendor`.\n204\t- Do NOT commit — dark-factory handles git.\n205\t- Existing tests must still pass, and the healthcheck / oauth-probe routing is untouched.\n206\t\n207\t</constraints>\n208\t\n209\t<verification>\n210\t\n211\tRun each command from the repo root. All must pass.\n212\t\n213\t```bash\n214\tmake test          # the new pkg/scripts suite runs here\n215\tmake precommit     # AC1 — must exit 0\n216\t\n217\t# AC9 (git half) — no push / commit / remote invocation anywhere in the scripts\n218\t! grep -nE 'git (push|commit|remote)' agent/scripts/*.sh\n219\t\n220\t# AC9 (curl half) — no curl invocation carries a write verb. The pipeline must print 0.\n221\ttest \"$(sed -e ':a' -e '/\\\\$/N; s/\\\\\\n//; ta' agent/scripts/*.sh | grep -E '(^|[^A-Za-z_])curl ' | grep -cE -- '(-X|--request|--upload-file| -T |--data([^-]|$)|--data-(binary|raw|ascii)|--json| -d | -F |--form)')\" = \"0\"\n222\t\n223\t# AC10 — no env knobs, no defaulted env vars. Both must find nothing.\n224\t! grep -qE 'REPO_CLONE_DIR|GIT_CLONE_DEPTH|GIT_CLONE_TOKEN|GATEWAY_SECRET' agent/scripts/*.sh\n225\t! grep -qE '\\$\\{[A-Z_]+:-' agent/scripts/*.sh\n226\t\n227\t# the script exists and is executable\n228\ttest -x agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh\n229\t\n230\t# the clone directory is ignored, and the test suite left no tree behind\n231\ttest \"$(grep -c '^/agent/repos/' .gitignore)\" = \"1\"\n232\ttest -z \"$(find agent/repos -mindepth 1 2>/dev/null)\"\n233\t```\n234\t\n235\t</verification>\n236\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"3e0ea873-6537-47ba-bd77-0eb17d068d8a","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:58:21.031Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b471fed728b5430d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n2\t// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n3\t// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n4\t\n5\t// Package factory wires concrete dependencies for the defect-diagnoser-agent binary.\n6\t//\n7\t// All factory functions follow the Create* prefix convention and contain\n8\t// zero business logic — they compose constructors with config.\n9\tpackage factory\n10\t\n11\timport (\n12\t\t\"context\"\n13\t\n14\t\tagentlib \"github.com/bborbe/agent\"\n15\t\tclaudelib \"github.com/bborbe/agent/claude\"\n16\t\tdelivery \"github.com/bborbe/agent/delivery\"\n17\t\thealthcheck \"github.com/bborbe/agent/healthcheck\"\n18\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/cqrs/base\"\n19\t\tlibkafka \"github.com/bborbe/kafka\"\n20\t\tlibtime \"github.com/bborbe/time\"\n21\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/vault-cli/pkg/domain\"\n22\t\n23\t\t\"github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/prompts\"\n24\t)\n25\t\n26\tconst serviceName = \"defect-diagnoser-agent\"\n27\t\n28\t// CreateClaudeRunner constructs a ClaudeRunner pre-configured with tools,\n29\t// model, working directory, and CLI environment.\n30\tfunc CreateClaudeRunner(\n31\t\tclaudeConfigDir claudelib.ClaudeConfigDir,\n32\t\tagentDir claudelib.AgentDir,\n33\t\tallowedTools claudelib.AllowedTools,\n34\t\tmodel claudelib.ClaudeModel,\n35\t\tenv map[string]string,\n36\t) claudelib.ClaudeRunner {\n37\t\treturn claudelib.NewClaudeRunner(claudelib.ClaudeRunnerConfig{\n38\t\t\tClaudeConfigDir:  claudeConfigDir,\n39\t\t\tAllowedTools:     allowedTools,\n40\t\t\tModel:            model,\n41\t\t\tWorkingDirectory: agentDir,\n42\t\t\tEnv:              env,\n43\t\t})\n44\t}\n45\t\n46\t// CreateSyncProducer creates a Kafka sync producer.\n47\tfunc CreateSyncProducer(\n48\t\tctx context.Context,\n49\t\tbrokers libkafka.Brokers,\n50\t) (libkafka.SyncProducer, error) {\n51\t\treturn libkafka.NewSyncProducerWithName(ctx, brokers, serviceName)\n52\t}\n53\t\n54\t// CreateKafkaResultDeliverer creates a ResultDeliverer that publishes task\n55\t// updates to Kafka via CQRS commands. Uses the passthrough content generator\n56\t// — the agent framework's StepRunner already produces the full marshaled\n57\t// task in result.Output; the deliverer publishes it as-is and overrides\n58\t// status/phase frontmatter based on the result Status.\n59\tfunc CreateKafkaResultDeliverer(\n60\t\tsyncProducer libkafka.SyncProducer,\n61\t\ttopicPrefix base.TopicPrefix,\n62\t\ttaskID agentlib.TaskIdentifier,\n63\t\toriginalContent string,\n64\t\tcurrentDateTime libtime.CurrentDateTimeGetter,\n65\t) agentlib.ResultDeliverer {\n66\t\treturn delivery.NewKafkaResultDeliverer(\n67\t\t\tsyncProducer,\n68\t\t\ttopicPrefix,\n69\t\t\ttaskID,\n70\t\t\toriginalContent,\n71\t\t\tdelivery.NewPassthroughContentGenerator(),\n72\t\t\tcurrentDateTime,\n73\t\t)\n74\t}\n75\t\n76\t// CreateFileResultDeliverer creates a ResultDeliverer that writes the agent's\n77\t// output back to a markdown file (local CLI mode). Uses the passthrough\n78\t// content generator (same rationale as Kafka).\n79\tfunc CreateFileResultDeliverer(filePath string) agentlib.ResultDeliverer {\n80\t\treturn delivery.NewFileResultDeliverer(\n81\t\t\tdelivery.NewPassthroughContentGenerator(),\n82\t\t\tfilePath,\n83\t\t)\n84\t}\n85\t\n86\t// CreateAgent assembles the full 3-phase claude agent. Single Claude step\n87\t// shared across planning / in_progress / ai_review preserves the existing\n88\t// CRD trigger.phases behavior — every phase runs Claude once and emits\n89\t// done.\n90\tfunc CreateAgent(\n91\t\tclaudeConfigDir claudelib.ClaudeConfigDir,\n92\t\tagentDir claudelib.AgentDir,\n93\t\tallowedTools claudelib.AllowedTools,\n94\t\tmodel claudelib.ClaudeModel,\n95\t\tclaudeEnv map[string]string,\n96\t\tenvContext map[string]string,\n97\t) *agentlib.Agent {\n98\t\treturn CreateAgentFromRunner(\n99\t\t\tCreateClaudeRunner(claudeConfigDir, agentDir, allowedTools, model, claudeEnv),\n100\t\t\tenvContext,\n101\t\t)\n102\t}\n103\t\n104\t// CreateAgentFromRunner builds the 3-phase claude agent given a pre-constructed\n105\t// ClaudeRunner. Used by CreateAgentProvider to share one runner across the\n106\t// domain agent and the healthcheck-Claude liveness agent.\n107\tfunc CreateAgentFromRunner(\n108\t\trunner claudelib.ClaudeRunner,\n109\t\tenvContext map[string]string,\n110\t) *agentlib.Agent {\n111\t\tstep := claudelib.NewAgentStep(claudelib.AgentStepConfig{\n112\t\t\tName:          \"claude-task\",\n113\t\t\tRunner:        runner,\n114\t\t\tInstructions:  prompts.BuildInstructions(),\n115\t\t\tEnvContext:    envContext,\n116\t\t\tOutputSection: \"## Result\",\n117\t\t\tNextPhase:     \"done\",\n118\t\t})\n119\t\treturn agentlib.NewAgent(\n120\t\t\tagentlib.NewPhase(\"planning\", step),\n121\t\t\tagentlib.NewPhase(domain.TaskPhaseExecution, step),\n122\t\t\tagentlib.NewPhase(\"ai_review\", step),\n123\t\t)\n124\t}\n125\t\n126\t// CreateAgentProvider wires the per-task-type dispatch table for defect-diagnoser-agent.\n127\t// Returns lib.AgentProvider — main.go calls Get(ctx, taskType) to select the\n128\t// appropriate *Agent. Pure plumbing; no conditional, no error.\n129\t//\n130\t// TaskTypeLLM routes to the existing 3-phase domain agent. TaskTypeHealthcheck\n131\t// and TaskTypeOAuthProbe (transition alias) both route to the shared\n132\t// healthcheck-Claude liveness agent, reusing the same ClaudeRunner.\n133\tfunc CreateAgentProvider(\n134\t\tclaudeConfigDir claudelib.ClaudeConfigDir,\n135\t\tagentDir claudelib.AgentDir,\n136\t\tallowedTools claudelib.AllowedTools,\n137\t\tmodel claudelib.ClaudeModel,\n138\t\tclaudeEnv map[string]string,\n139\t\tenvContext map[string]string,\n140\t) agentlib.AgentProvider {\n141\t\trunner := CreateClaudeRunner(claudeConfigDir, agentDir, allowedTools, model, claudeEnv)\n142\t\tdomainAgent := CreateAgentFromRunner(runner, envContext)\n143\t\tlivenessAgent := healthcheck.NewAgent(healthcheck.NewClaudeStep(runner))\n144\t\treturn agentlib.NewAgentProvider(serviceName, map[agentlib.TaskType]*agentlib.Agent{\n145\t\t\tagentlib.TaskTypeLLM:         domainAgent,\n146\t\t\tagentlib.TaskTypeHealthcheck: livenessAgent,\n147\t\t\tagentlib.TaskTypeOAuthProbe:  livenessAgent,\n148\t\t})\n149\t}\n150\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"1907eb5c-709a-4030-ba44-da480c2214a3","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:58:21.032Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
