{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-919a8d79af04b40c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Definition of Done\n2\t\n3\tAfter completing your implementation, review your own changes against each criterion below. These are quality checks you perform by inspecting your work — not commands to run (linting and tests already ran via `validationCommand`). Report any unmet criterion as a blocker.\n4\t\n5\t## Code Quality\n6\t\n7\t- Exported types, functions, and interfaces have doc comments\n8\t- Error handling follows project conventions (no silently ignored errors)\n9\t- No debug output (print statements, fmt.Printf) — use structured logging\n10\t\n11\t## Testing\n12\t\n13\t- New code has good test coverage (target >= 80%)\n14\t- Changes to existing code have tests covering at least the changed behavior\n15\t\n16\t## Dependencies\n17\t\n18\t- If `make precommit` fails due to a dependency vulnerability with a known fix version, update the dependency (`go get <pkg>@<fixed-version> && go mod tidy && go mod vendor`) as part of your change\n19\t- No `exclude` or `replace` directives in go.mod (break remote install)\n20\t\n21\t## Documentation\n22\t\n23\t- README.md is updated if the change affects usage, configuration, or setup\n24\t- Documentation is updated if the change affects behavior described in docs/ (notably `docs/observation-scripts.md` and `docs/verdict-gate.md`)\n25\t- When changing CLI args, config fields, env vars, or flags (add, rename, remove, change default), grep the entire repo and update all references in docs/, README.md, examples, and comments\n26\t- CHANGELOG.md has an entry under `## Unreleased`\n27\t- New or changed integration seam (per the dark-factory scenario-writing rules, \"When to Write a Scenario\") → scenario under `scenarios/` added or updated\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"91f15841-9186-4f8d-871b-4d6d8c558