{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a962c0f4fcfab4b7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Observation scripts — contracts\n2\t\n3\tThe diagnoser observes the running system only through these read-only scripts. **This page is the authoritative contract** for them; the upstream scripts they were ported from (named at the end) are informational only.\n4\t\n5\tThe Config's `ALLOWED_TOOLS` grants each script as `Bash(scripts/<name>.sh:*)`, and Claude invokes them relative to its working directory (the agent dir, `/agent` in the image). They live in `agent/scripts/` and ship through the Dockerfile's `COPY agent/ /agent/`.\n6\t\n7\tContract source: [[Defect Lane Task Chain]] § Live observation — read path 1 (task files) and read path 2 (metrics). Read path 3 (Kubernetes API) waits on a platform change and has no script.\n8\t\n9\t## How the scripts get their env\n10\t\n11\tThe Claude runner passes only `HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,ZONEINFO,TMPDIR,LANG,LC_ALL` from the pod into the Claude subprocess. `GIT_REST_URL` and `PROMETHEUS_URL` reach the scripts through the existing `CLAUDE_ENV` channel (comma-separated `KEY=VALUE`, merged into `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` by both entry points):\n12\t\n13\t- in-cluster: Config `spec.env.CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"`\n14\t- local CLI: `-claude-env='GIT_REST_URL=…,PROMETHEUS_URL=…'`\n15\t\n16\tAt `-v=2` the runner logs `cmd.Env = [...]`; both keys appear there when forwarding works.\n17\t\n18\t## Common rules (all three HTTP scripts)\n19\t\n20\t| Rule | Value |\n21\t|---|---|\n22\t| Method | `GET` only — no `-X`, `--request`, `-d`, `--data`, `--data-raw`, `--data-binary`, `--json`, `-F`, `--form`, `-T`, `--upload-file`; query parameters go through `-G --data-urlencode` |\n23\t| Timeout | `--max-time 30` |\n24\t| HTTP error | non-zero exit; stderr carries the HTTP status (e.g. `500`, `401`) — curl `-sS -f` or an explicit status check |\n25\t| Missing env var | non-zero exit; stderr names the variable (`<VAR> is required`) |\n26\t| Output cap | stdout capped at 65536 bytes; when cut, stderr contains `truncated` and the exit code is **0** (the cut must not surface as a pipefail / SIGPIPE failure) |\n27\t| Env | only the variable named below; no defaulted (`${VAR:-…}`) env knobs, no gateway secret, no tokens |\n28\t\n29\t## `vault-read.sh <path>`\n30\t\n31\t- One argument: a vault-relative file path.\n32\t- Rejected with exit 2 and no request: absolute path (leading `/`), any `..` segment (`../b.md`, `a/../b.md`, `a/..`), any `?`, `#` or `://`.\n33\t- Spaces are percent-encoded.\n34\t- Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/<encoded path>`.\n35\t- Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n36\t\n37\t## `vault-list.sh <glob>`\n38\t\n39\t- One argument: a git-rest glob (`filepath.Match` semantics; `*` does not cross `/`; `**` unsupported).\n40\t- Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/` with query parameter `glob=<glob>` (URL-encoded).\n41\t- stdout: one path per line; empty when nothing matches.\n42\t- Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n43\t\n44\t## `prometheus-query.sh <promql>`\n45\t\n46\t- Exactly one argument: a PromQL instant-query expression.\n47\t- Rejected with exit 2 and no request: an argument starting with `/` or containing `://`.\n48\t- Request: `GET ${PROMETHEUS_URL}/api/v1/query` with query parameter `query=<promql>` (URL-encoded). The path is fixed; no other Prometheus path is reachable. No `time` parameter — Prometheus evaluates at its own now.\n49\t- Env: `PROMETHEUS_URL`.\n50\t\n51\t## `repo-clone.sh clone <repo>`\n52\t\n53\t- The only subcommand is `clone`. Anything else (including `log`) → exit 2 with usage on stderr.\n54\t- `<repo>` accepts `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>[.git]`, `git@github.com:<owner>/<name>.git`, or `<owner>/<name>`. It is normalized to `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>`.\n55\t- Validation, before git runs or the filesystem is touched — exit 2 on failure:\n56\t  - `owner` and `name` each match `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` (so `bborbe/.github` is valid)\n57\t  - neither `owner` nor `name` is `.` or `..` (so `../x`, `x/..`, `x/.`, `./.`, `../..` are invalid)\n58\t  - **defense in depth:** the destination `<agent dir>/repos/<owner>/<name>`, resolved to an absolute path with symlinks followed, lies strictly inside `<agent dir>/repos/`. This is checked before any `rm -rf` or `chmod`, and catches a pre-existing symlink under `repos/` pointing outside it.\n59\t- Clone root is fixed: the `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` (`/agent/repos` in the image; `agent/repos/` in a local checkout, gitignored). No env override.\n60\t- Clone: full history, no `--recurse-submodules`, no credentials (public repos only in v1).\n61\t- Replacing an existing clone first restores owner write permission on the old tree, then removes it — so re-cloning over a read-only tree succeeds for a non-root user.\n62\t- After cloning, the whole tree including `.git` is made non-writable (`chmod -R a-w`).\n63\t- stdout (flat `key=value`): `clone_path=<absolute path>`, `head_sha=<sha>`, `default_branch=<branch>`.\n64\t- `git clone` failure (any non-zero exit, e.g. 128) → non-zero exit, stderr `git clone failed for <url>`.\n65\t\n66\tCleanup after a local run: `chmod -R u+w agent/repos && rm -rf agent/repos`.\n67\t\n68\t## Upstream (informational only)\n69\t\n70\tPorted from `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/vault-list.sh`, `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/repo-clone.sh` (whose `..` traversal hole this contract closes), and `trading/agent/trade-analysis/agent/scripts/vault-read.sh`. `prometheus-query.sh` is new. Where this page and an upstream script disagree, this page wins.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"a8f86dfd-7cbb-4397-96ba-4f5e5233f2ed","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:59:55.032Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c216760cc44a11d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Scenario 001: diagnose one observed defect\n2\t\n3\t**Purpose**: prove the agent turns one operator observation into a `## Verdict` with a `file:line` that resolves, verified against the running system. Run before any deploy; run again after any non-trivial change.\n4\t\n5\t**Setup**:\n6\t- Agent `bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent` deployed to dev\n7\t- Config CRD applied: `kubectlnukedev -n dev get config.agent.benjamin-borbe.de defect-diagnoser-agent` shows it\n8\t- The applied Config's `ENV_CONTEXT` holds one `service_repo.<service>=<owner>/<repo>` entry for the defect's service (exact, case-sensitive name). This mapping is operator-supplied at apply time and is never committed to this repo's `k8s/` (see `docs/verdict-gate.md` § mapping input)\n9\t- One real, currently reproducible defect in a dev service (read paths 1–2 only: task files, Prometheus — pod logs wait on the platform change, see NEXT-DIRECTIONS)\n10\t\n11\t**Acceptance**: the task ends `completed` with a `## Verdict` whose `file:line` exists at the cloned ref and whose `evidence` quotes a live read that shows the misbehaviour.\n12\t\n13\t## Steps\n14\t\n15\t1. **Create the task** (operator writes the task file directly — `vault-cli` has no task-create command; the intake-surface task will later replace this step with the one-gesture command):\n16\t   ```bash\n17\t   SLUG=\"<short-slug>\"\n18\t   DEFECT_ID=\"defect-$(date +%Y%m%d)-${SLUG}\"\n19\t   cat > ~/Documents/Obsidian/Personal/\"25 Tasks/Defect ${SLUG}.md\" <<EOF\n20\t   ---\n21\t   task_type: defect-diagnose\n22\t   assignee: defect-diagnoser-agent\n23\t   status: in_progress\n24\t   phase: planning\n25\t   defect_id: ${DEFECT_ID}\n26\t   ---\n27\t\n28\t   ## Observation\n29\t\n30\t   <what misbehaved, in the operator's own words, naming the running service>\n31\t   EOF\n32\t   ```\n33\t   (Write the heredoc lines without the list indentation.) The `## Observation` is the operator's own words. **No root cause, no suspected component, no `file:line`.** The service it names must match the `service_repo.` entry from Setup exactly.\n34\t\n35\t2. **Observe controller pickup**:\n36\t   ```bash\n37\t   kubectlnukedev -n dev logs agent-task-controller-personal-0 --tail=200 | grep \"<task_identifier>\"\n38\t   ```\n39\t   Expected: the task is published within one poll cycle.\n40\t\n41\t3. **Observe executor spawn**:\n42\t   ```bash\n43\t   kubectlnukedev -n dev get pods | grep defect-diagnoser-agent\n44\t   ```\n45\t   Expected: a Job pod appears within 30s of the publish.\n46\t\n47\t4. **Verify the task file**:\n48\t   Expected:\n49\t   - Frontmatter `status: completed`. An escalation (`assignee: \"\"` with a `## Failure`) is a legitimate outcome of the diagnoser's escalation path, but it fails this happy-path scenario.\n50\t   - Body has `## Verdict` with a yaml block carrying `defect_id`, `service`, `repo`, `file:line`, `root_cause`, `recommended_fix`, `evidence`, `confidence: High`\n51\t\n52\t## Pass criteria\n53\t\n54\t- [ ] Task reaches `status: completed` with no `## Failure` section\n55\t- [ ] `file:line` resolves: `git -C <clone> show <ref>:<path> | sed -n '<line>p'` prints a non-empty line (the pod's clone is ephemeral, so `<clone>` is a local clone of the verdict's `repo`, and `<ref>` is the `head_sha` recorded in the task's `## Plan`)\n56\t- [ ] `evidence` quotes a script call **and its output**, and that output shows the observed misbehaviour\n57\t- [ ] The `## Observation` still contains no root cause, component, or `file:line` (operator supplied no diagnosis)\n58\t- [ ] No agent-pipeline alerts fired in the 10 min after completion\n59\t\n60\t## Fail recovery\n61\t\n62\tIf the task fails (`## Failure`, or `assignee: \"\"`):\n63\t1. Read the `## Failure` / escalation reason for the error class\n64\t2. Common classes: transient infra (retry), missing script or env (preflight gap — see [[Fail-Fast Preflight for Tool-Dependent LLM Agents]]), service did not resolve to a repo (mapping gap — escalate, do not invent), defect not reproducible (expected `needs_input`)\n65\t3. Re-trigger: `vault-cli task set \"<title>\" assignee defect-diagnoser-agent`\n66\t\n67\t## Related\n68\t\n69\t- [[Defect Diagnoser Agent]] — agent knowledge page\n70\t- [[Defect Lane Task Chain]] — the contract this agent implements\n71\t- [[Agent Pipeline Debug Guide]]\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"650eee62-9e0c-4180-8a27-903ca6708b83","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:59:55.033Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
