{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4c783f40bb8d31d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tinclude tools.env\n2\t\n3\tdefault: precommit\n4\t\n5\tprecommit: ensure format generate test check addlicense\n6\t\t@echo \"ready to commit\"\n7\t\n8\tensure:\n9\t\tgo mod tidy\n10\t\tgo mod verify\n11\t\trm -rf vendor\n12\t\n13\tformat:\n14\t\tfind . -type f -name 'go.mod' -not -path './vendor/*' -exec go run github.com/shoenig/go-modtool@$(GO_MODTOOL_VERSION) -w fmt \"{}\" \\;\n15\t\tgo run github.com/incu6us/goimports-reviser/v3@$(GOIMPORTS_REVISER_VERSION) -project-name github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent -format -excludes vendor ./...\n16\t\tfind . -type d -name vendor -prune -o -type f -name '*.go' -print0 | xargs -0 -n 10 go run github.com/segmentio/golines@$(GOLINES_VERSION) --max-len=100 -w\n17\t\tfind . -type f -name '*.go' -not -path './vendor/*' -exec gofmt -w \"{}\" +\n18\t\n19\tgenerate:\n20\t\trm -rf mocks avro\n21\t\tmkdir -p mocks\n22\t\techo \"package mocks\" > mocks/mocks.go\n23\t\tgo generate -mod=mod ./...\n24\t\n25\t.PHONY: generatek8s\n26\tgeneratek8s:\n27\t\tbash hack/update-codegen.sh\n28\t\n29\t# -race=true catches data races but flakes on some CI runners (rare SIGSEGV\n30\t# during gexec.Build in cmd/*-style binary smoke tests). Default off; opt in\n31\t# via ENABLE_RACE=true for nightly/manual hardening runs.\n32\tTESTFLAGS_RACE = -race=false\n33\tifdef ENABLE_RACE\n34\t\tTESTFLAGS_RACE = -race=true\n35\tendif\n36\t\n37\t.PHONY: test\n38\ttest:\n39\t\tgo test -mod=mod -p=$${GO_TEST_PARALLEL:-1} -cover $(TESTFLAGS_RACE) $(shell go list -mod=mod ./... | grep -v /vendor/)\n40\t\n41\tcheck: lint vet errcheck vulncheck osv-scanner gosec trivy\n42\t\n43\tlint:\n44\t\tgo run github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2/cmd/golangci-lint@$(GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION) run --allow-parallel-runners --config .golangci.yml ./...\n45\t\n46\tvet:\n47\t\tgo vet -mod=mod $(shell go list -mod=mod ./... | grep -v /vendor/)\n48\t\n49\terrcheck:\n50\t\tGODEBUG=gotypesalias=1 go run github.com/kisielk/errcheck@$(ERRCHECK_VERSION) -ignore '(Close|Write|Fprint)' $(shell go list -mod=mod ./... | grep -v /vendor/ | grep -v k8s/client)\n51\t\n52\tVULNCHECK_IGNORE ?= GO-2026-4923 GO-2026-4514 GO-2022-0470 GO-2026-4772 GO-2026-4771 GO-2026-5932 GO-2026-5064 GO-2026-5338 GO-2026-5622\n53\t\n54\t.PHONY: vulncheck\n55\tvulncheck:\n56\t\t@PKGS=\"$(shell go list -mod=mod ./... | grep -v /vendor/)\"; \\\n57\t\tIGNORE_JSON=$$(printf '%s\\n' $(VULNCHECK_IGNORE) | jq -R . | jq -s .); \\\n58\t\tREMAIN=$$(go run golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@$(GOVULNCHECK_VERSION) -format json $$PKGS 2>/dev/null | \\\n59\t\t\tjq -rs --argjson ignore \"$$IGNORE_JSON\" \\\n60\t\t\t\t'(map(select(.osv != null)) | map({key: .osv.id, value: (.osv.summary // \"\")}) | from_entries) as $$sum | \\\n61\t\t\t\t map(select(.finding != null) | .finding) | \\\n62\t\t\t\t map(select(.osv as $$o | $$ignore | index($$o) | not)) | \\\n63\t\t\t\t map(\"\\(.osv)\\t\\(.trace[-1].module)@\\(.trace[-1].version) -> \\(.fixed_version)\\t\\($$sum[.osv] // \"\")\") | \\\n64\t\t\t\t unique | .[]'); \\\n65\t\tif [ -n \"$$REMAIN\" ]; then \\\n66\t\t\techo \"Unexpected vulnerabilities (ignored: $(VULNCHECK_IGNORE)):\"; \\\n67\t\t\tprintf '%s\\n' \"$$REMAIN\" | column -t -s \"$$(printf '\\t')\"; \\\n68\t\t\texit 1; \\\n69\t\telse \\\n70\t\t\techo \"No unignored vulnerabilities found\"; \\\n71\t\tfi\n72\t\n73\tosv-scanner:\n74\t\t@if [ -f .osv-scanner.toml ]; then \\\n75\t\t\techo \"Using .osv-scanner.toml\"; \\\n76\t\t\tgo run github.com/google/osv-scanner/v2/cmd/osv-scanner@$(OSV_SCANNER_VERSION) --config .osv-scanner.toml --recursive .; \\\n77\t\telse \\\n78\t\t\techo \"No config found, running default scan\"; \\\n79\t\t\tgo run github.com/google/osv-scanner/v2/cmd/osv-scanner@$(OSV_SCANNER_VERSION) --recursive .; \\\n80\t\tfi\n81\t\n82\tgosec:\n83\t\tgo run github.com/securego/gosec/v2/cmd/gosec@$(GOSEC_VERSION) -exclude=G104 ./...\n84\t\n85\t.PHONY: trivy\n86\ttrivy:\n87\t\ttrivy fs \\\n88\t\t--db-repository ghcr.io/aquasecurity/trivy-db \\\n89\t\t$(if $(wildcard .trivyignore),--ignorefile .trivyignore,$(if $(wildcard $(ROOTDIR)/.trivyignore),--ignorefile $(ROOTDIR)/.trivyignore,)) \\\n90\t\t$(if $(wildcard .trivy-secret.yaml),--secret-config .trivy-secret.yaml,$(if $(wildcard $(ROOTDIR)/.trivy-secret.yaml),--secret-config $(ROOTDIR)/.trivy-secret.yaml,)) \\\n91\t\t--scanners vuln,secret \\\n92\t\t--skip-dirs vendor \\\n93\t\t--quiet \\\n94\t\t--no-progress \\\n95\t\t--disable-telemetry \\\n96\t\t--exit-code 1 .\n97\t\n98\taddlicense:\n99\t\tgo run github.com/google/addlicense@$(ADDLICENSE_VERSION) -c \"Benjamin Borbe\" -y $$(date +'%Y') -l bsd $$(find . -name \"*.go\" -not -path './vendor/*')\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"61ed2a09-470b-4000-875c-d84ca8663908","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:59:59.911Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b617b17771ce9c7d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Defect Diagnoser Agent\n2\t\n3\t**Stage 1 of the defect lane** ([[Defect Lane Task Chain]]). Takes a `task_type: defect-diagnose` task — the operator's `## Observation` of a misbehaving service, with no diagnosis attached — and writes a `## Verdict` with a root cause and a `file:line`, verified against the running system rather than inferred from source.\n4\t\n5\t- **Input:** `## Observation` (operator's words only — no root cause, component or `file:line`)\n6\t- **Output:** `## Verdict` yaml block — `defect_id`, `service`, `repo`, `file:line`, `root_cause`, `recommended_fix`, `evidence`, `confidence`\n7\t- **Observes (read-only, in order):** task files → Prometheus → pod logs/events via its own read-only service account\n8\t- **Escalates** (`needs_input`) instead of guessing when the defect cannot be reproduced or `confidence` is below High\n9\t\n10\tScaffolded from the `bborbe/agent-claude` template via `/launch-agent` on 2026-09-27; the domain logic below the template scaffolding is not implemented yet.\n11\t\n12\t## How It Works\n13\t\n14\t1. Agent pipeline ([[task/controller]] → Kafka → [[task/executor]]) spawns a K8s Job with the `defect-diagnoser-agent` image.\n15\t2. The Job receives `TASK_CONTENT`, `TASK_ID`, `BRANCH`, `ALLOWED_TOOLS`, `MODEL`, etc. via env vars.\n16\t3. `main.go` assembles the prompt via `lib/claude` (embedded `workflow.md` + `output-format.md` + task content).\n17\t4. Runs `claude --print --output-format stream-json` with the allowed tools.\n18\t5. Parses the JSON result and publishes to Kafka via `lib/delivery.KafkaResultDeliverer` (when `TASK_ID` set), or falls back to `NoopResultDeliverer` for local runs.\n19\t\n20\t## Env Vars\n21\t\n22\t| Var | Required | Default | Purpose |\n23\t|---|---|---|---|\n24\t| `TASK_CONTENT` | yes | — | Raw task markdown |\n25\t| `BRANCH` | yes | — | `dev`/`prod` — used as Kafka topic prefix |\n26\t| `TASK_ID` | no | — | Required when publishing results via Kafka |\n27\t| `MODEL` | no | `sonnet` | `sonnet` or `opus` |\n28\t| `ALLOWED_TOOLS` | no | — | Comma-separated Claude tool allowlist (e.g. `Read,Grep,Bash`) |\n29\t| `AGENT_DIR` | no | `agent` | Directory containing `.claude/CLAUDE.md` guardrails |\n30\t| `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` | no | — | Claude Code OAuth config directory (PVC mount) |\n31\t| `ENV_CONTEXT` | no | — | Comma-separated `KEY=VAL` pairs injected into the prompt |\n32\t| `CLAUDE_ENV` | no | — | Comma-separated `KEY=VAL` pairs passed to the Claude CLI subprocess |\n33\t| `KAFKA_BROKERS` | no | — | Required when `TASK_ID` is set |\n34\t| `SENTRY_DSN` | no | — | Error reporting |\n35\t\n36\t## Creating a New Agent\n37\t\n38\tTo add a domain-specific agent that reuses this binary:\n39\t\n40\t1. Create a task file in OpenClaw vault with `assignee: claude-agent` (or a new assignee routed to this image via a Config CRD).\n41\t2. Mount a PVC or Secret containing the domain-specific `.claude/CLAUDE.md` and any API credentials.\n42\t3. Set `ALLOWED_TOOLS` on the Config CRD to the minimum tools the agent needs.\n43\t4. Set `ENV_CONTEXT` to inject domain context (e.g. API URLs) into the prompt without modifying the binary.\n44\t\n45\t### Config CRD env pattern\n46\t\n47\tThe `Config` CRD's `spec.env` map becomes pod env vars, which `main.go` consumes via struct tags. Example from `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`:\n48\t\n49\t```yaml\n50\tspec:\n51\t  env:\n52\t    ALLOWED_TOOLS: WebSearch,WebFetch,Read,Grep\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\tTune `ALLOWED_TOOLS` per task shape (minimum viable set):\n56\t\n57\t| Task shape | Minimum tools |\n58\t|---|---|\n59\t| Web research | `WebSearch,WebFetch,Read,Grep` |\n60\t| Vault I/O via scripts | `Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-write.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Grep` |\n61\t| API query via script | `Bash(scripts/trading-api-read.sh:*),Grep` |\n62\t| Code edit | `Read,Write,Edit,Grep,Glob,Bash(go:*),Bash(make:*)` |\n63\t\n64\tPrefer constrained `Bash(path:*)` forms over bare `Bash` to minimize shell attack surface.\n65\t\n66\t### Claude subprocess env allowlist\n67\t\n68\t`lib/claude/claude-runner.go` strips pod env down to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...`) before spawning `claude`. Custom env vars (API URLs, credentials) **must** be threaded explicitly via `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env map[string]string` in `main.go`. Don't expect pod env to reach Claude by default. See `docs/` for precedent (trade-analysis commit `1ccfa674cf`).\n69\t\n70\t## Local Quick Test\n71\t\n72\t```bash\n73\tcd ~/Documents/workspaces/agent/agent/claude\n74\tgo run . \\\n75\t  --task-content \"$(cat /path/to/task.md)\" \\\n76\t  --model sonnet \\\n77\t  --allowed-tools \"Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob\" \\\n78\t  --agent-dir agent \\\n79\t  --branch dev\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\tSkips K8s, task controller, task executor, git writeback. Useful for iterating on prompts.\n83\t\n84\t## Links\n85\t\n86\tAdmin endpoints:\n87\t- Dev: <https://dev.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/defect-diagnoser-agent/setloglevel/3>\n88\t- Prod: <https://prod.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/defect-diagnoser-agent/setloglevel/3>\n89\t\n90\t## Related\n91\t\n92\t- `pkg/prompts/` — embedded prompts (`workflow.md`, `output-format.md`)\n93\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — default agent guardrails\n94\t- `docs/claude-oauth-setup.md` — seed PVC with Claude Code OAuth credentials\n95\t- `lib/claude/` — shared prompt assembly + Claude CLI invocation\n96\t- `lib/delivery/` — shared Kafka result publishing\n97\t- `task/controller/` — Obsidian→Kafka event source\n98\t- `task/executor/` — Kafka→K8s Job spawner\n99\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"8a314b81-3add-4fc2-804e-08ad4a322065","timestamp":"2026-09-27T22:59:59.912Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
